Adapt RDO's rpm-master openstack-neutron.spec to the released 2026.1 tarball
(neutron 28.0.2).

The fifth instance of the same upstream change (after keystone, placement, nova
and os-ken): the generated WSGI scripts are gone. Diffing the spec's %files
against what neutron 28.0.2's pyproject.toml actually declares leaves exactly
two entries unaccounted for:

    error: File not found: .../usr/bin/neutron-api
    error: File not found: .../usr/bin/neutron-server

Everything else the spec packages is still declared. neutron 28.0.2 ships
neutron/wsgi/api.py instead, and keeps neutron-rpc-server,
neutron-periodic-workers, neutron-ovn-metadata-agent and the rest as real
console scripts.

WHAT THIS PATCH DELIBERATELY DOES NOT FIX: the distgit also ships
neutron-server.service with

    ExecStart=/usr/bin/neutron-server --config-file ... --config-dir ...

which now points at a binary that does not exist. As with nova, running the API
on 2026.1 means a WSGI server against neutron.wsgi.api - which is exactly the
shape Ubuntu 26.04 already uses, where the networking API is an Apache vhost and
only neutron-rpc-server and neutron-periodic-workers are units. A Rocky
hagistack would write its own httpd configuration rather than enable this unit.

F-NEW-1: THE OVN MAINTENANCE-WORKER LOCK RACE

This patch also adds two upstream Neutron commits to the build, as Patch0001
and Patch0002. The two patch files are created next to the spec:

    83f1d8305651a0ab23629c88d70bfa237055158c
        Ensure MaintenanceWorker lock set before connect
    91abb5e720e1c515dbfbe9b2313fbdff92b2abbf
        Only set the maintenance worker lock on the worker (LP #2156979)

Both are on master and stable/2026.2, not on stable/2026.1. In 28.0.2 the
maintenance worker calls Idl.set_lock() from its main thread while the OVSDB
connection thread is already running Idl.run(). The lock reply can be read and
dropped in between, and the worker then runs for ever without the lock: every
write to the northbound database fails with NOT_LOCKED while systemd reports
the unit active. 0001 requests the lock before the connection starts. 0002
restricts that request to the real maintenance worker. On 2026.1 the RPC
workers share the code path 0001 changes, so 0001 without 0002 would make them
request the maintenance lock too. The two are carried together, never apart.

The files are `git format-patch --zero-commit` output of the two upstream
commits cherry-picked onto the 28.0.2 tag. Their changed lines are the
upstream lines; one context line differs from upstream. The spec's
`%autosetup -S git` applies them.

diff -ur a/neutron/openstack-neutron.spec b/neutron/openstack-neutron.spec
--- a/openstack-neutron.spec	2026-09-28 21:43:16
+++ b/openstack-neutron.spec	2026-09-28 23:25:25
@@ -63,6 +63,12 @@
 Source101:        https://tarballs.openstack.org/%{service}/%{service}-%{upstream_version}.tar.gz.asc
 Source102:        https://releases.openstack.org/_static/%{sources_gpg_sign}.txt
 %endif
+
+# Hagistack: upstream fix for the OVN maintenance-worker lock race, which is
+# not in stable/2026.1. Rebased onto 28.0.2. The two are carried together:
+# 0001 alone would make RPC workers request the maintenance lock as well.
+Patch0001:      0001-Ensure-MaintenanceWorker-lock-set-before-connect.patch
+Patch0002:      0002-Only-set-the-maintenance-worker-lock-on-the-worker.patch
 
 BuildArch:      noarch
 
@@ -654,7 +660,6 @@
 
 %files
 %license LICENSE
-%{_bindir}/neutron-api
 %{_bindir}/neutron-db-manage
 %{_bindir}/neutron-dhcp-agent
 %{_bindir}/neutron-ipset-cleanup
@@ -667,7 +672,6 @@
 %{_bindir}/neutron-remove-duplicated-port-bindings
 %{_bindir}/neutron-sanity-check
 %{_bindir}/neutron-status
-%{_bindir}/neutron-server
 %{_bindir}/neutron-usage-audit
 %{_bindir}/neutron-ovn-metadata-agent
 %{_bindir}/neutron-ovn-agent
diff --git a/0001-Ensure-MaintenanceWorker-lock-set-before-connect.patch b/0001-Ensure-MaintenanceWorker-lock-set-before-connect.patch
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/0001-Ensure-MaintenanceWorker-lock-set-before-connect.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,70 @@
+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Terry Wilson <twilson@redhat.com>
+Date: Tue, 9 Jun 2026 17:33:16 -0500
+Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Ensure MaintenanceWorker lock set before connect
+
+The Idl.set_lock() call sets the lock name on the Idl class and
+sends a request to ovsdb-server requesting a lock. It does not
+wait for a reply. This creates a window where we run without
+yet receiving the lock, and tasks might fire and fail and have
+to be retried.
+
+If set_lock() is called prior to connection, the reply that
+contains the initial database dump wil aslo have the reply to the
+set_lock request, so we eliminate that window.
+
+Related-Bug: #2155155
+Change-Id: Iaefe1e2cc86ddd55c9053fde66353b2a333e1e98
+Signed-off-by: Terry Wilson <twilson@redhat.com>
+(cherry picked from commit 83f1d8305651a0ab23629c88d70bfa237055158c)
+---
+ neutron/common/ovn/constants.py                                | 1 +
+ .../plugins/ml2/drivers/ovn/mech_driver/ovsdb/impl_idl_ovn.py  | 1 +
+ .../plugins/ml2/drivers/ovn/mech_driver/ovsdb/maintenance.py   | 3 ---
+ 3 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
+
+diff --git a/neutron/common/ovn/constants.py b/neutron/common/ovn/constants.py
+index ddf1f494c2..640d737970 100644
+--- a/neutron/common/ovn/constants.py
++++ b/neutron/common/ovn/constants.py
+@@ -289,6 +289,7 @@ TYPES_PRIORITY_ORDER = (
+ DB_CONSISTENCY_CHECK_INTERVAL = 300  # 5 minutes
+ MAINTENANCE_TASK_RETRY_LIMIT = 100  # times
+ MAINTENANCE_ONE_RUN_TASK_SPACING = 5  # seconds
++MAINTENANCE_NB_IDL_LOCK_NAME = "ovn_db_inconsistencies_periodics"
+ 
+ # The addresses field to set in the logical switch port which has a
+ # peer router port (connecting to the logical router).
+diff --git a/neutron/plugins/ml2/drivers/ovn/mech_driver/ovsdb/impl_idl_ovn.py b/neutron/plugins/ml2/drivers/ovn/mech_driver/ovsdb/impl_idl_ovn.py
+index 3ee09db6bf..0303892598 100644
+--- a/neutron/plugins/ml2/drivers/ovn/mech_driver/ovsdb/impl_idl_ovn.py
++++ b/neutron/plugins/ml2/drivers/ovn/mech_driver/ovsdb/impl_idl_ovn.py
+@@ -245,6 +245,7 @@ class OvsdbNbOvnIdl(nb_impl_idl.OvnNbApiIdlImpl, Backend):
+         if worker_class in (worker.MaintenanceWorker,
+                             n_service.RpcWorker):
+             idl_ = ovsdb_monitor.BaseOvnIdl.from_server(*args)
++            idl_.set_lock(ovn_const.MAINTENANCE_NB_IDL_LOCK_NAME)
+         else:
+             idl_ = ovsdb_monitor.OvnNbIdl.from_server(*args, driver=driver)
+         conn = connection.Connection(idl_, timeout=cfg.get_ovn_ovsdb_timeout())
+diff --git a/neutron/plugins/ml2/drivers/ovn/mech_driver/ovsdb/maintenance.py b/neutron/plugins/ml2/drivers/ovn/mech_driver/ovsdb/maintenance.py
+index c4552043b5..433e9a60b3 100644
+--- a/neutron/plugins/ml2/drivers/ovn/mech_driver/ovsdb/maintenance.py
++++ b/neutron/plugins/ml2/drivers/ovn/mech_driver/ovsdb/maintenance.py
+@@ -54,8 +54,6 @@ LOG = log.getLogger(__name__)
+ 
+ INCONSISTENCY_TYPE_CREATE_UPDATE = 'create/update'
+ INCONSISTENCY_TYPE_DELETE = 'delete'
+-# TODO(bpetermann): move MAINTENANCE_NB_IDL_LOCK_NAME to neutron-lib
+-MAINTENANCE_NB_IDL_LOCK_NAME = "ovn_db_inconsistencies_periodics"
+ 
+ 
+ def has_lock_periodic(*args, periodic_run_limit=0, **kwargs):
+@@ -232,7 +230,6 @@ class DBInconsistenciesPeriodics(SchemaAwarePeriodicsBase):
+         self._nb_idl = self._ovn_client._nb_idl
+         self._sb_idl = self._ovn_client._sb_idl
+         self._idl = self._nb_idl.idl
+-        self._idl.set_lock(MAINTENANCE_NB_IDL_LOCK_NAME)
+         super().__init__(ovn_client)
+ 
+         self._resources_func_map = {
diff --git a/0002-Only-set-the-maintenance-worker-lock-on-the-worker.patch b/0002-Only-set-the-maintenance-worker-lock-on-the-worker.patch
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/0002-Only-set-the-maintenance-worker-lock-on-the-worker.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Terry Wilson <twilson@redhat.com>
+Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 18:45:25 -0500
+Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Only set the maintenance worker lock on the worker
+
+Other code passes the MaintenanceWorker as the trigger to
+from_server() like the ovn-db-sync-util and only the real
+MaintenanceWorker itself should call set_lock() before
+connecting.
+
+Closes-Bug: #2156979
+
+Signed-off-by: Terry Wilson <twilson@redhat.com>
+Change-Id: I74145ef1407856b7ec75de87daa2270b452b6c70
+(cherry picked from commit 91abb5e720e1c515dbfbe9b2313fbdff92b2abbf)
+---
+ neutron/plugins/ml2/drivers/ovn/mech_driver/mech_driver.py   | 3 +++
+ .../ml2/drivers/ovn/mech_driver/ovsdb/impl_idl_ovn.py        | 5 ++++-
+ 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
+
+diff --git a/neutron/plugins/ml2/drivers/ovn/mech_driver/mech_driver.py b/neutron/plugins/ml2/drivers/ovn/mech_driver/mech_driver.py
+index 08accf1910..1cd376966b 100644
+--- a/neutron/plugins/ml2/drivers/ovn/mech_driver/mech_driver.py
++++ b/neutron/plugins/ml2/drivers/ovn/mech_driver/mech_driver.py
+@@ -427,6 +427,9 @@ class OVNMechanismDriver(api.MechanismDriver):
+         if worker_class == wsgi.WorkerService:
+             self._setup_hash_ring()
+ 
++        if worker_class == worker.MaintenanceWorker:
++            worker_class.lock_name = ovn_const.MAINTENANCE_NB_IDL_LOCK_NAME
++
+         # Initialize singleton agent cache and keep a copy.
+         self._agent_cache = n_agent.AgentCache(self)
+         self.nb_ovn, self.sb_ovn = impl_idl_ovn.get_ovn_idls(self, trigger)
+diff --git a/neutron/plugins/ml2/drivers/ovn/mech_driver/ovsdb/impl_idl_ovn.py b/neutron/plugins/ml2/drivers/ovn/mech_driver/ovsdb/impl_idl_ovn.py
+index 0303892598..6f5c3b3464 100644
+--- a/neutron/plugins/ml2/drivers/ovn/mech_driver/ovsdb/impl_idl_ovn.py
++++ b/neutron/plugins/ml2/drivers/ovn/mech_driver/ovsdb/impl_idl_ovn.py
+@@ -245,7 +245,10 @@ class OvsdbNbOvnIdl(nb_impl_idl.OvnNbApiIdlImpl, Backend):
+         if worker_class in (worker.MaintenanceWorker,
+                             n_service.RpcWorker):
+             idl_ = ovsdb_monitor.BaseOvnIdl.from_server(*args)
+-            idl_.set_lock(ovn_const.MAINTENANCE_NB_IDL_LOCK_NAME)
++            try:
++                idl_.set_lock(worker_class.lock_name)
++            except AttributeError:
++                pass
+         else:
+             idl_ = ovsdb_monitor.OvnNbIdl.from_server(*args, driver=driver)
+         conn = connection.Connection(idl_, timeout=cfg.get_ovn_ovsdb_timeout())
